<title>UK: NNPC says crude export cancellations imminent.</title>
<headline>NNPC says crude export cancellations imminent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian National Petroleum Corp (NNPC) will have to start cancelling crude export shipments if community disturbances extend into the weekend, an NNPC official said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>NNPC's leading joint venture partner Royal Dutch/Shell already has warned that it expects to declare force majeure on crude cargoes loading in the first 20 days of April.</p>
<p>Shell has been forced to reduce output by 210,000 bpd from the Forcados and Bonny fields. The force majeure is expected to delay Shell shipments by two or three days apiece, the NNPC official said.</p>
<p>Output was first hit last Saturday after villagers occupied crude flow stations in the Niger delta oil producing region.</p>
<p>-- Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
